viogpudo: the vertical blank at the EDID's rate.

On top of 01-vsync.  With no VSyncHz in the registry the blank's rate is
the device's EDID's: its preferred timing (the first detailed timing
descriptor, the pixel clock over the total size), which 2ksbox's player
sets to a rate dividing the host screen's (embed API v15; 72 Hz on a
144 Hz screen, 60 on a 60 or 120 Hz one).  It is read when the device
starts and again on each display event, whose EDID the driver now fetches
for it; a new rate restarts the timer's schedule at the next blank, and
the modes report it as mHz over 1000.  60 Hz when the device gives no
EDID.  VSyncHz in the registry still sets the rate (0: upstream's
behaviour).  (QEMU's EDID says 75 Hz when no front end gives a rate.)

